  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Define the operation \\(\\star\\) by \\(a\\star b = (a+b)b.\\) What is \\((3\\star 5)-(5\\star 3)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-16\\)",
    "B": "\\(-8\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(16\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "In the definition, the multiplier is the second input, so evaluate each ordered pair separately:\n\\[\n3\\star5=(3+5)5=40,\n\\qquad\n5\\star3=(5+3)3=24.\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\n(3\\star5)-(5\\star3)=40-24=\\boxed{16},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
